   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## MOSS Image Prompt \u2014 example\n\nTwo reference images, each with its **own strength**, read by MOSS-Image's text encoder (no VAE, no LoRA).\n\n1. Put `example_watercolor.jpg` and `example_pulp_monster.jpg` (in this pack's `example_workflows/` folder) into the two **Load Image** nodes \u2014 drag them in, or copy them to `ComfyUI/input`.\n2. Run. The watercolor (`strength_1` 0.10) sets the medium; the monster (`strength_2` 0.12) brings in its subject.\n3. Move **`strength_2`**: about 0.05 = no monster, 0.20 = the monster takes over and the watercolor fades.\n\n**Strengths:** 1 = unweighted (swamps the prompt), ~0.01\u20130.15 = useful range, 0 = image left out. They're relative: compare images' strengths to each other, and raise **`text_strength`** (2\u20133) if your words get lost.\n\n**`vision_size`:** how big the encoder sees each image (384 like core). Bigger = more detail and more pull.\n\nWire **info** to see the tokens and bias per part. Keep the negative on a plain CLIP Text Encode.\n\n## Models ([Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image))\n\n- diffusion_models: [moss_image_sft_int8_convrot.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image/resolve/main/diffusion_models/moss_image_sft_int8_convrot.safetensors)\n- text_encoders: [qwen3.5_9b_w4a8_gptq.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image/resolve/main/text_encoders/qwen3.5_9b_w4a8_gptq.safetensors)\n- vae: [flux2-vae_small.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MOSS-Image/resolve/main/vae/flux2-vae_small.safetensors)\n"
   ]
  }
